1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,570
Quarantine. Proof, not claims. Every pip
install runs someone else's code before
anyone has read it. This one runs it inside a
container that cannot reach the network,
cannot write outside its folder, and has no
root — and then shows you what it tried.

2
00:00:15,370 --> 00:00:18,870
Seven runs, five packages, three of them
blocked.

3
00:00:19,670 --> 00:00:29,200
harborline 2.9.1. It builds and imports
cleanly, and still comes back high. Keep that
in mind: it is the whole point of the next two
runs.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:46,390
Because its problem is not its own code, it is
what it pins. urllib3 1.24.1, a release from
2018, thirteen known advisories, the worst
scored eight out of ten. The threshold is
seven. The wheels are fetched and hashed,
never installed.

5
00:00:47,190 --> 00:01:00,890
Dependencies are half of it. This package has
none. Its install hook tried to reach a host,
write outside its own directory, and read an
SSH key. The sandbox denied all three — and
every denial points at a file you can open.

6
00:01:01,690 --> 00:01:13,670
And this one builds clean, imports clean, and
only on import spawns a process and calls
home. A dependency scanner would have passed
it. That is why there are three phases, and
why the import phase is not optional.

7
00:01:14,470 --> 00:01:27,290
Every claim in the report cites something that
exists in this run: the proxy log, the process
result, the filesystem diff. The model may
summarise them, never exceed them — a claim
pointing at a source that is not here gets
dropped.

8
00:01:28,090 --> 00:01:40,910
The threshold is a setting, not a constant. So
is the model, the reasoning budget, and how
many runs one address may start per hour. And
the honest part: accounts are demo-only, and
the delete button is deliberately inert.

9
00:01:41,710 --> 00:01:53,850
The architecture in three sentences: a VM runs
the control plane, every task gets its own
hardened container, and the verdict is built
from evidence the container cannot write to.
MIT, ninety-six tests.

10
00:01:54,650 --> 00:01:57,340
Quarantine. Live at this URL.
